{"id": "EUVD-2026-82222", "enisaUuid": "b6082b09-cf9b-30bf-a0f6-f3832413e5bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/surface: acpi-notify: Check ACPI companion before use\n\nSince every platform driver can be forced to match a device that doesn't\nmatch its list of device IDs because of device_match_driver_override(),\nplatform drivers that rely on the existence of a device's ACPI companion\nobject should verify its presence.\n\nsan_probe() dereferences the result of ACPI_COMPANION() when installing\nthe GSBUS address space handler, so force-binding the driver to a device\nwithout an ACPI companion leads to a NULL pointer dereference.  The\ndereference was introduced when the probe function was switched from\nACPI_HANDLE() to ACPI_COMPANION().\n\nCheck the ACPI companion against NULL and return -ENODEV when it is\nmissing, like commit e4865a56d013 (\"ACPI: driver: Check ACPI_COMPANION()\nagainst NULL during probe\") does for the core ACPI platform drivers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4faa43d4ef0b98beb6c2b77a279f4aa5d7fa2d13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3855be0100efb98c26228c610db70a673611f3bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f276b62f2ce1cbff7fa50a8ee5afd8fef5a60897", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b6479da662c2ec4e931ed9f7228df46aa8c3766", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7fea5a310e3b2db24f7aafe64897e4e659ffbb7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/428a82d987fcd8844e8868c85582eae75b4b5c51", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b3a5dabe89e330413af403246b648c1890f368f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93114", "GHSA-fmfr-wc4p-75cj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14e34ef2-770c-3fbc-9fd3-2cf56e14ce20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <4faa43d4ef0b98beb6c2b77a279f4aa5d7fa2d13"}, {"id": "18424a34-9ed8-3b40-a3f4-d4ff31481119", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <2b3a5dabe89e330413af403246b648c1890f368f"}, {"id": "38879eac-489b-313b-8981-3770428caed1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "4e03e07e-95b3-3991-9ff4-fd1bfaa34033", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "5016b07c-2212-3322-8d07-fbc21538723c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <7fea5a310e3b2db24f7aafe64897e4e659ffbb7d"}, {"id": "7135c311-ead7-35c7-b86b-7c0b98bbef1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <9b6479da662c2ec4e931ed9f7228df46aa8c3766"}, {"id": "8b64c221-bbe2-3e7f-a7ea-fed201d4f7de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "a164bda3-fa68-3959-9f30-cb1d3cecbd27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <3855be0100efb98c26228c610db70a673611f3bd"}, {"id": "a8615e4c-be3f-3255-94ef-5709e034e7b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "b2601d9b-803f-3d9c-ba76-04a2cf10b7c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "b492813d-2610-3c11-8cf4-127cba2702f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <428a82d987fcd8844e8868c85582eae75b4b5c51"}, {"id": "c0d7b2b6-cc46-3b59-b49a-0521707a8604", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9e10e58730432e5de840eb3ddd55c75f29341b3 <f276b62f2ce1cbff7fa50a8ee5afd8fef5a60897"}, {"id": "c38afdff-bc2e